# Root-level bin/linux-<arch>/ is the PREBUILT bundle layout the flake's
# short-circuit consumes (flake.nix:prebuiltBinDir). It must NEVER be committed:
# a git flake only sees tracked files, so an uncommitted bin/ keeps in-repo
# builds (self-hosting `yolo -- bash`) compiling from source. A committed bin/
# would silently force every source build into stale prebuilt binaries — the
# exact source drift this design eliminates. Only shipped/baked path: bundles
# carry bin/, never the repo.
/bin/
# Stray root-level Go build artifacts: a bare `go build ./cmd/<x>` or
# `go build ./tools/<x>` drops the binary here. The real build channel is
# dist-go/; these should never be tracked (a stale root yolo-parity was committed
# once). One line per directory under cmd/ and tools/, no more and no fewer —
# internal/entrypoint/rootbinaryignore_test.go fails in either direction.
/goprobe
/yolo
/yolo-cglimit
/yolo-entrypoint
/yolo-jaild
/yolo-journalctl
/yolo-ps
/yolo-serial
/build-wheels
.DS_Store
.research/
yolo-jail.local.jsonc

